-- DBTITLE 1,Genie
-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### 3.7 ⑦ Genie AI
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Genie is Databricks' AI-powered data assistant. Instead of writing a query, you type a question like *"How many pupils were enrolled in 2023?"* and Genie generates and runs the SQL for you, returning results and a plain-English explanation. It's connected directly to Unity Catalog, so it understands your actual table structures and column names. It can also be used as an assistant to write or translate code, but you must still be able to understand, test, explain and maintain it.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Genie is useful for:
-- MAGIC - Quick one-off questions where you don't want to write a full query
-- MAGIC - Exploring an unfamiliar dataset to understand what's in it
-- MAGIC - Non-technical users who need answers from data without writing SQL
-- MAGIC - Help fix bugs in code
-- MAGIC - Translating code (e.g. SQL to R), use this with caution, only small sections at a time, and sense check!
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC It's not a replacement for writing your own code. For anything complex, you should use the SQL Editor or a notebook. But it's a handy starting point.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ---
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ### ✅ Task: Try Genie
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Genie** in the top right
-- MAGIC 2. Ask it a question about a table you found in the Catalog (e.g. *"What columns does this table have?"* or *"Show me the first 10 rows of [table name]"*)
-- MAGIC 3. Did it generate SQL automatically? Did the results look correct?

