-- DBTITLE 1,Cloning and Connecting to DevOps
-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## 4. How to clone repos and connect to Azure DevOps or GitHub
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Databricks integrates with Azure DevOps and GitHub for version control.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ### How to clone a repo
-- MAGIC 1. In the left sidebar, click **Workspace** > navigate to your user Home folder
-- MAGIC 2. Click  **Create** > **Git folder**
-- MAGIC 3. Paste the **clone URL** from your Azure DevOps or GitHub repo 
-- MAGIC 4. Select provider as Azure DevOps or GitHub accordingly 
-- MAGIC 5. Give your folder a name and click **Create Git folder**
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ![Cloning Repo](data:image/png;base64,)
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ### Key points
-- MAGIC - Each user clones their own copy of the repo into their workspace
-- MAGIC - Changes are committed and pushed back to DevOps or Github just like any other Git workflow
-- MAGIC - You can create branches, pull, commit, and push from the Git dialog in Databricks
-- MAGIC - The `.gitignore` file which tells Git which files or folders to deliberately ignore and not track, is respected
-- MAGIC - Notebooks are saved as source files (`.py`, `.sql`, `.r`), not proprietary formats
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ### Tips
-- MAGIC - Always **pull** before starting work to get the latest changes
-- MAGIC - Use meaningful commit messages
-- MAGIC - Avoid working directly on `main`, create feature branches
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ----
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ### Creating or changing to another branch 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC To create a new branch, you first navigate to your cloned repo and next to the repo name you will see the current branch you are in, you will most likely be in the `main` branch. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC ![Changing git branch](data:image/png;base64,)
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Clicking on the branch name will pop up a screen where you can see the edits you made, a drop down for all the other branches in this area which you are able to click and change over, you can pull the data and also create a branch here too. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC
